.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt HOSTNAME 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm hostname
.Nd print or set the system hostname
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar name
.Nm
.Fl -selftest
.Sh DESCRIPTION
With no operand,
.Nm
reads
.Pa sys:/hostname
and prints the current hostname.
With one
.Ar name ,
it writes the name to
.Pa sys:/hostname
through the
.Xr sysd 8
server.  The name must be non-empty, at most 64 bytes, and contain no NUL,
.Ql / ,
or control characters.
.Pp
The protocol version 1 hostname is stored by
.Xr sysd 8
and is not persisted across a reboot.
.Pp
.Fl -selftest
reads the current value, sets
.Ql selftest-host ,
verifies it, restores the original value, and prints
.Dq hostname: selftest ok .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A usage error exits with status 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr uname 1 ,
.Xr sysd 8
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Nm
interface follows the traditional BSD utility.
